course: dictionary
lesson: 9389
title: Spreading, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Spreading is the -ing form of the verb spread. Spread can mean covering a surface, opening something out, or getting bigger. The words around it show which meaning you need. «Spreading butter on toast» means covering, and «a fire spreading» means getting bigger.
explain: Look for clues. «Fire doors must stay closed to stop smoke and fire spreading.» The word stop tells you that spreading is something bad we want to prevent, so it means getting bigger and reaching more places. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Spreading can also mean sharing things out. «Spreading the work» means dividing it so more people each do a part. «Spreading the word» means telling lots of people. The phrase gives you the clue.
explain: Sometimes a spreading mark is a warning. «A spreading red area, fever or red lines up the arm need a doctor quickly.» A red mark that is getting bigger is a sign to tell a grown-up straight away.
fact: Spreading is the -ing form of the verb spread: spread, spreads, spread, spreading.
fact: «Spreading» can mean covering something with a thin layer, as in «spreading butter».
fact: «Spreading» can mean getting bigger or reaching more places, as in «a fire spreading» or «germs spreading».
fact: Germs spread from person to person through coughs, sneezes and dirty hands, so washing your hands helps stop them spreading.
fact: Rumours spreading can hurt people, so do not pass on news you cannot check.
exercise: Sam is «spreading jam on his toast». What does spreading mean here? | Breaking into small pieces | Opening out to full size | *Covering a surface with a thin layer | Getting bigger and reaching more places
exercise: «Fire doors must stay closed to stop smoke and fire spreading.» What does spreading mean here? | Covering a surface with a thin layer | Opening out to full size | *Getting bigger and reaching more places
exercise: «Spreading the work» means | *Sharing it out so more people help | Making the work bigger and harder | Hiding it under a blanket
test: A bird is spreading its wings. What does spreading mean? | Sharing out work | Covering a surface | *Opening something out to its full size | Getting smaller
test: Why should you not pass on rumours? | Because they are funny | Because they are always true | *Because spreading rumours can hurt people
exam: Read this: «A spreading red ring days after a tick bite means a doctor should check it.» What does spreading mean here? | *Getting bigger, so it needs checking | Covering with butter | Opening out like a map | Sharing out the cost
